# HeroOS local environment template.
# Never place real credentials in this file.

# Required, no default: development | staging | production.
# The API refuses to start if it is missing.
HEROOS_ENV=development

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Local PostgreSQL development database (docs/operations/database-credentials.md).
# Never type or commit database passwords: `make env-init` copies this file to
# the untracked root .env (mode 0600) and generates every value left empty below.
# `make env-check` validates .env without printing values. There are no
# built-in defaults: empty values stop Docker Compose, Alembic and the API.
#
# Staging and production credentials must come from secure environment configuration
# (AWS Secrets Manager; not yet provisioned). Outside development the API refuses to
# start unless DATABASE_URL is set explicitly to a non-local host, and it
# refuses MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL entirely (the API never holds the admin role).
#
# Docker Compose: password of the migration/admin role `heroos` (POSTGRES_PASSWORD)
# and of the API runtime role `heroos_app` (the api container's DATABASE_URL).
HEROOS_DB_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
HEROOS_DB_APP_PASSWORD=
# Host tooling. DATABASE_URL is the API runtime role: not superuser, no
# BYPASSRLS, owns no tables, so PostgreSQL Row-Level Security applies. The API
# refuses to start with a privileged role. Create/update it with `make db-runtime-role`.
DATABASE_URL=
# Migration/admin role that owns the schema. Used by Alembic only, never the API.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=

# Authentication (see docs/architecture/authentication.md).
# development | cognito. Unset means every protected request is rejected.
# The development provider is refused at startup unless HEROOS_ENV=development;
# staging and production require cognito.
HEROOS_AUTH_PROVIDER=development

# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Signs local dev bearer tokens (`make dev-token
# SUBJECT=...`), so anyone holding it can mint tokens: generated by
# `make env-init`, never committed. Staging and production refuse to start if
# this variable is set at all.
HEROOS_DEV_AUTH_SECRET=

# Amazon Cognito access-token verification (deployed environments; no pool exists yet).
# Required when HEROOS_AUTH_PROVIDER=cognito. Never commit real values here.
# HEROOS_COGNITO_ISSUER=https://cognito-idp.<region>.amazonaws.com/<user-pool-id>
# HEROOS_COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID=<app-client-id>
# Optional; defaults to <issuer>/.well-known/jwks.json
# HEROOS_COGNITO_JWKS_URI=
# Optional resource-server identifier. When set, access tokens must carry a
# matching `aud`; when unset, `aud` is not checked.
# HEROOS_COGNITO_RESOURCE_AUDIENCE=

# Private object storage (see docs/architecture/private-object-storage.md).
# local | s3. Unset means no object storage: every object operation is refused.
# `local` is development only and refused in staging/production. `s3` is the
# production contract and stops startup until its adapter exists.
# HEROOS_STORAGE_PROVIDER=local
# Required for `local`: an ABSOLUTE path outside the repository and outside any
# web-served directory. Created with 0700 directories and 0600 files.
# HEROOS_LOCAL_STORAGE_ROOT=/absolute/path/outside/the/repository/heroos-private-objects
